WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.240
Want a message to go out by itself, again and again?

2
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:10.382
In Send a message, write your daily signal.

3
00:00:10.682 --> 00:00:12.211
Tap "🔁 Repeat".

4
00:00:12.341 --> 00:00:15.583
Pick "Weekdays", and set the time to 9:00 AM.

5
00:00:16.405 --> 00:00:18.164
Ends: "On a date".

6
00:00:18.294 --> 00:00:22.047
The chips show your next sends, so you always know when it goes.

7
00:00:22.346 --> 00:00:26.035
To keep it fresh, tap "Add a version", and write another one.

8
00:00:26.165 --> 00:00:29.855
Make three, and they take turns, in order or at random.

9
00:00:34.777 --> 00:00:36.680
Add a voice note too.

10
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.875
Tap "🎙️ Voice", then hold the microphone, and talk.

11
00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:44.341
Play it back.

12
00:00:44.471 --> 00:00:45.696
Happy?

13
00:00:45.826 --> 00:00:47.371
Tap "Use this".

14
00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.090
Round videos work the same way.

15
00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.995
Tap "⭕ Round" to use your front camera, or upload a short clip.

16
00:00:54.293 --> 00:00:56.121
Open "More options".

17
00:00:56.251 --> 00:01:00.010
"Delete this message after…" 24 hours, and "Pin it".

18
00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:01.701
Tap save.

19
00:01:01.831 --> 00:01:07.024
Your repeating message gets its own card, with the next send, pause, and history.

20
00:01:07.323 --> 00:01:10.618
And on the calendar, every coming send is waiting.

21
00:01:10.748 --> 00:01:14.101
That's it: your messages now go out by themselves.
